Analysis

Project Requirements

The Safarino project was designed in Adobe XD with the aim of creating a modern and user-friendly travel application interface. The main objective of this project is to improve the user experience by providing a simple, organized, and visually attractive environment for accessing different travel services.

The project focuses on designing mobile application screens rather than implementing the application. Therefore, all pages were created to demonstrate the complete user journey and interaction with the interface.

Functional Requirements

User Login

User Registration

OTP Verification

Password Login

User Profile

Home Page

Search Function

Recommended Hotels

Nearby Hotels

My Trips

Safarino Pro


Non-Functional Requirements

Simple and clean interface

Consistent visual identity

Mobile-first design

Easy navigation

Readable typography

Consistent use of colors and icons



---

Project Analysis

The interface was designed to reduce user confusion and make navigation between different sections simple and intuitive. All pages follow the same visual style to create consistency throughout the application.

Special attention was given to screen layouts, spacing, typography, icon placement, and color harmony. Green was selected as the primary color because it represents nature, travel, and comfort, while neutral colors were used to improve readability.

The design process also focused on organizing information in a clear hierarchy so users could quickly identify the most important elements on each screen.


---

User Flow

The application workflow is designed as follows:

1. Open the application.


2. Log in using a mobile number or password.


3. Verify the account using the OTP code if required.


4. Access the Home page.


5. Search for destinations or browse available travel services.


6. View recommended or nearby hotels.


7. Access the "My Trips" section to manage travel history.


8. Explore additional features through the Safarino Pro section.


9. Navigate easily between different screens using the bottom navigation bar.




---

Design Decisions

Several design principles were considered during the development of this project:

Creating a simple and understandable interface.

Maintaining visual consistency across all pages.

Using readable typography and standard icons.

Organizing information with a clear visual hierarchy.

Providing quick access to the main sections of the application.

Designing every page based on mobile user experience principles.


These decisions helped create a modern interface that is easy to learn, visually balanced, and comfortable for users.